ty"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Release cadences that make quarterly Western updates look sluggish"}]]}],["$","p","265",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Business Model Maturation"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Pricing power and revenue growth proving sustainability"}]]}],["$","p","266",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"4. "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"Global Ambition"}],["$","span","2",{"children":": Open-source releases and API availability designed for worldwide adoption"}]]}],["$","p","268",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"For international observers, the question is no longer \"Can China compete in AI?\"—that question has been definitively answered. The new question is: \"How will global AI competition evolve when multiple centers of excellence challenge Western leadership?\""}]]}],["$","p","270",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"April 2026 suggests the answer will be: faster, more competitive, and more globally distributed than previously assumed."}]]}],["$","hr","272",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","margin":"32px 0"}}],["$","p","274",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*AI in China tracks the most significant developments in Chinese artificial intelligence, from cutting-edge research to commercial deployment. For more analysis, subscribe to our weekly briefing.*"}]]}],["$","hr","277",{"style":{"border":"none","borderTop":"1px solid #1a1a1a","mar